## Workplanes

Always call .workplane() after selecting a face before placing 2D geometry.

```python
result = (
    cq.Workplane("XY")
    .box(20, 20, 10)
    .faces(">Z").workplane()
    .circle(5).extrude(8)
)
```

centerOption controls where the workplane origin lands. The default
"ProjectedOrigin" is often not the face center. Set it explicitly
when position matters:

```python
solid.faces(">Z").workplane(centerOption="CenterOfBoundBox").circle(3).extrude(5)
```

After .workplane(), all coordinates are local to that plane, not global.

